post.description:
The statement the approver's passkey signs: "gvnr-approve-v1
{graph}
{node}
{run}
{account}
{head seq}
{head hash}
{nonce}" (the plan's newest step when the approval began); challenge is its SHA-256, base64url. allow lists the caller's passkeys for this site. 409 no_passkey when they have none; 400 invalid_body from a site GVNR does not allow; 404 for a plan, task or run the caller cannot see. A person only.

Checks navigator.credentials.create's answer against the challenge from begin (once, 5 minutes): the site, the origin, the person verified on the device (fingerprint, face or PIN), and the credential id. Stores the public key (SPKI from response.getPublicKey(); ES256, EdDSA or RS256) and GVNR's seal over "gvnr-passkey-v1
{account}
{credential}
{sha256 of the key}
{created_at}". 400 invalid_body for anything that does not check out; 409 already_exists for a passkey already added.

state.description:
State is judged (a call was made and read), skipped (nothing was sent;
Reason says why) or unavailable (the call failed; the row was stored
plainly with review=false).

attempts.description:
Attempts counts calls that could not cast a vote (judge unavailable);
the re-judge worker stops retrying at its MaxAttempts and the run's
deadline escalates it. A token cap or an unusable key is not counted.

